Ukraine has dismissed Russia's calls for  a 36-hour ceasefire as a ploy President  Putin has told his troops to observe a  truce which has come into effect this  morning and it's to Mark Orthodox  Christmas but Kiev says that it won't be  following saying that Russia will only  get a ceasefire when it leaves Ukrainian  territory  now the Russians want to use Christmas  as a cover to stop the advance of our  guys in the donbass for a while and to  bring in equipment ammunition and  mobilize people closer to our positions  what will it result in just another  increase in their losses  well our International correspondent  Alex Rossi joins us live he's in fastiv  which is southwest of Kiev Alex good to  see you this afternoon  um any evidence of even a one-sided  ceasefire  well certainly from Russia's uh position  they are saying that they will maintain  a unilateral ceasefire this was ordered  by Vladimir Putin yesterday telling his  defense minister Sergey shoigu to hand  down the order to troops along the line  of contact but we are hearing reports  that there is shelling going on along as  hundreds of miles of trenches where the  fighting is taking place there were also  Air Raid Sirens going off where we were  we're in Kiev when it came into effect  at 12 o'clock so a few hours ago we  heard the air raid sirens we didn't hear  any sounds of explosions and none had  been reported but those Air Raid Sirens  we understand were sounding around the  country as you can imagine there is  profound suspicion here of Russia's  motives if anything at the moment  Ukraine has the momentum it has the  initiative and they see this really as  just a ploy by the Russians to buy them  time so that they can reinforce their  troops in positions where they are  facing a fairly desperate situation it's  a chance to strengthen their logistic  lines bring ammunition up to the front  so although it's been rejected by the  ukrainians they haven't said that they  they will or they won't fire him which I  suppose is indicative of the fact as a  part of a military strategy why would  you signal to the enemy uh what you are  or are not going to do but one would  expect that it will carry on one other  word though it's very very cold anyway  and because of the festivities you would  expect the tempo of the fighting perhaps  to calm down in many places as a result  of that but certainly the ukrainians  profoundly suspicious and that they have  rejected what Vladimir Putin has offered  as this ceasefire ostensibly for  Orthodox Christmas and they say the only  truce that Russia is ever going to get  is if it withdraws completely from  Ukrainian territory
 

